        timingType: "Chain (Located at the FRONT of the engine block. The M57 timing chain system is universally regarded as one of the most reliable architectures ever produced by BMW. Unlike the later N57 engine, which moved the chain to the inaccessible rear and suffered from snapping issues, the M57's front-mounted dual-chain setup is massively over-engineered. It is a genuine lifetime component that rarely requires servicing, often outlasting the vehicle chassis itself, provided that standard 10,000 km oil change intervals are respected.)", injectionType: "Common Rail Direct Injection (Equipped with a highly robust Bosch CP3 high-pressure fuel pump and generation 2 Piezo injectors. Operating at 1,600 bar, this system provides excellent atomization for the heavy X6 chassis. The CP3 pump is legendary for its durability, virtually immune to the catastrophic implosions that plagued later CP4 models. However, the Piezo injectors can suffer from tip degradation over high mileage, causing uneven spray patterns that lead to piston melting if ignored. Frequent fuel filter changes are mandatory.)", engineLifespan: "500,000+ km (The M57TU2 is widely considered the absolute pinnacle of BMW diesel reliability. It is a legendary workhorse. If the fatal flaw of the intake manifold swirl flaps is addressed by blanking them off, and the thermostats are maintained to allow DPF regenerations, the closed-deck aluminum block and forged internals will easily surpass half a million kilometers without breaking a sweat.)", turboType: "Single Variable Geometry Turbocharger (VGT). (Fitted with an incredibly durable Garrett GT2260VK turbocharger. The electronic actuator adjusts the exhaust vanes in real-time, providing a massive 520Nm surge of torque from very low RPMs, effectively masking the immense 2.2-ton weight of the E71 X6. The turbo core is practically indestructible if supplied with clean oil and allowed to cool after heavy loads.)", ecuType: "Bosch EDC16 (An older, yet incredibly stable and highly deciphered engine management system. It controls the VGT, EGR, and DPF parameters. The EDC16 is an absolute dream for tuners, allowing for massive power increases via simple OBD-II port flashing without the need for bench unlocking or bypassing complex modern security layers.)", euroStandard: "Euro 4", maxPowerStockInternals: "400 - 450 hp (The M57TU2 block, featuring forged connecting rods and an over-engineered crankshaft, is virtually indestructible. A simple Stage 1 tune safely extracts 290hp. With an upgraded hybrid turbocharger and a larger intercooler, the stock bottom end will comfortably handle well over 400hp and 800Nm of torque without flinching, making it one of the greatest diesel tuning platforms in the world.)",
