          "Turbocharger Destruction (Clogged DPF): If the thermostats fail and the engine runs cold, the DPF will become completely blocked with soot. This creates a massive exhaust backpressure wall, forcing extreme heat directly back into the turbocharger housing, cooking the bearings and destroying the turbo.",
