        sisterModels: [ { name: "BMW X5 M60i (G05 LCI)", note: "The heavily related G05 X5 M60i LCI utilizes the exact same S68 engine with 48V mild-hybrid integration. The immense DIY knowledge base regarding the Heat Management Module, Dual Injection system, and FEMTO ECU tuning translates perfectly to this X6." } ],
        tuningPotential: [
          { stage: "Stage 1 (FEMTO Unlock + Bootmod3 / MHD Flash)", power: "650 - 680 hp", notes: "THE ULTIMATE UPGRADE. The S68 is an absolute tuning monster, but the Bosch ECU is heavily encrypted. You MUST physically remove the ECU and ship it to FEMTO in Finland for a bench unlock. Once unlocked, a simple OBD flash safely unlocks a massive amount of hidden power, jumping from 530hp to over 650hp and 900Nm of torque. The factory reinforced ZF 8-speed transmission handles this effortlessly.", zeroToHundred: "3.7s", hundredToTwoHundred: "8.5s" },
          { stage: "Stage 2 (Downpipes & Tune)", power: "700 - 750 hp", notes: "Requires high-flow or catless downpipes. The exhaust note becomes incredibly aggressive. Thanks to the new Dual Injection system and high-pressure fuel pumps, fueling is no longer a bottleneck. The closed-deck S68 block handles this power brilliantly, providing a massive wave of mid-range torque.", zeroToHundred: "3.4s", hundredToTwoHundred: "7.5s" },
          { stage: "Stage 3 (Upgraded Turbos)", power: "850 - 900+ hp", notes: "Requires upgrading the factory turbos to hybrid units and running E85 blends. The S68 closed-deck block and forged crankshaft can safely handle immense power on stock internals. The Dual Injection system allows for massive fuel delivery without complicated auxiliary fuel setups. This turns the M60i into an absolute hypercar killer.", zeroToHundred: "2.9s", hundredToTwoHundred: "6.2s" }
        ],
        tuningGraphData: { stock: { hp: 530, nm: 750 }, stage1: { hp: 680, nm: 900 }, stage2: { hp: 750, nm: 950 }, stage3: { hp: 900, nm: 1100 } },
