        sisterModels: [ { name: "BMW X5 40i (G05 LCI)", note: "The incredibly popular G05 X5 40i LCI utilizes the exact same B58TU2 engine with 48V mild-hybrid integration. The immense DIY knowledge base regarding the PCV diaphragm, Heat Management Module, Dual Injection system, and FEMTO ECU tuning translates perfectly to this X7." } ],
        tuningPotential: [
          { stage: "Stage 1 (FEMTO Unlock + Bootmod3 / MHD Flash)", power: "440 - 460 hp", notes: "THE ULTIMATE UPGRADE. The B58TU2 is an absolute tuning monster, but the Bosch MG1 ECU is heavily encrypted. You MUST physically remove the ECU and ship it to FEMTO in Finland for a bench unlock. Once unlocked, a simple OBD flash safely unlocks a massive amount of hidden power, jumping from 381hp to over 450hp and 600Nm of torque. The factory ZF 8-speed transmission handles this effortlessly.", zeroToHundred: "5.0s", hundredToTwoHundred: "12.5s" },
          { stage: "Stage 2 (Downpipes & Tune)", power: "480 - 500 hp", notes: "Requires a high-flow or catless downpipe. The exhaust note becomes incredibly aggressive. Thanks to the new Dual Injection system and factory TU high-pressure fuel pump, fueling is no longer a bottleneck. The closed-deck B58 block handles this power brilliantly, providing a massive wave of mid-range torque.", zeroToHundred: "4.6s", hundredToTwoHundred: "11.0s" },
          { stage: "Stage 3 (Upgraded Turbo)", power: "600 - 700+ hp", notes: "Requires upgrading the factory turbo to a hybrid unit (e.g., Pure800) and running E85 blends. The B58 closed-deck block and forged crankshaft can safely handle 650+ hp on stock internals, making it a true modern 2JZ. The Dual Injection system allows for massive fuel delivery without complicated auxiliary fuel setups.", zeroToHundred: "4.0s", hundredToTwoHundred: "9.5s" }
        ],
